# Run the API (`dotnet run --project src/Benefits.Employees.Api`) then send these from
# Visual Studio, Rider or VS Code (REST Client extension).
@host = http://localhost:5080

### Add a new starter -> 201 Created + Location header
# @name create
POST {{host}}/api/v1/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Mr",
  "firstName": "Dili",
  "surname": "Okoye",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-05-17",
  "gender": "Male",
  "email": "dili.okoye@gmail.com",
  "address": {
    "line1": "1 High Street",
    "line2": "Flat 2",
    "town": "Derby",
    "county": "Derbyshire",
    "postcode": "de1 1aa"
  }
}

### Fetch the employee just created -> 200 OK
GET {{host}}/api/v1/employees/{{create.response.body.employeeNo}}

### Same email, different case -> 409 Conflict
POST {{host}}/api/v1/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Mr",
  "firstName": "Dili",
  "surname": "Okoye",
  "dateOfBirth": "1988-01-02",
  "gender": "Male",
  "email": "DILI.OKOYE@gmail.com",
  "address": { "line1": "2 High Street", "town": "Derby", "postcode": "DE1 1AB" }
}

### Invalid details -> 400 with an error per field
POST {{host}}/api/v1/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "King",
  "dateOfBirth": "2015-01-01",
  "gender": "1",
  "email": "nope",
  "address": { "postcode": "XYZ" }
}

### Unknown employee -> 404
GET {{host}}/api/v1/employees/EMP999999
